    },
    {
      "claim": "L5 gut-wall efflux records are mechanism-level and not F measurements: imatinib is an efflux substrate (C60,C63,C65,C69) and tandutinib efflux restricts intestinal absorption (C62,C64,C66), but no L5 card reports an absolute F value; efflux substrate status alone does not establish F<20%.",
      "card_ids": ["C60","C62","C63","C64","C65","C66","C69"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "L5 also includes high passive permeability and saturable efflux for MMB, a 2-anilinopyrimidine (C61,C67,C70,C71), which supports absorption but is not query-specific; C68 (dabigatran not a P-gp substrate) is not transferable to the query scaffold.",
      "card_ids": ["C61","C67","C70","C71","C68"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "The calculated low-neutral-fraction prior is not an experimental F measurement and is outweighed by direct human F values in structurally related contexts (C08,C10,C19).",
      "card_ids": ["C08","C10","C19"]
    }
