    }
  ],
  "evidence_gaps": [
    "No direct absolute oral bioavailability measurement exists for the query molecule.",
    "No human PK, dose, formulation, or prandial-state data are available for the query.",
    "No query-specific permeability or solubility measurements were supplied; L4 contains only solubility/dissolution records for other scaffolds.",
    "No query-specific gut-wall efflux or intestinal metabolism data were supplied; L5 records are for dabigatran, imatinib, tandutinib, and MMB.",
    "No intestinal metabolism records were actually supplied in L5; all L5 cards are transport/efflux records.",
    "The low neutral-fraction prior is calculated, not experimentally confirmed; high ionization could increase solubility while reducing passive permeability, and transporter-mediated absorption is unmeasured."
  ],
  "decision_summary": "Predicted high because direct human absolute F values in the most transferable structural contexts (nilotinib ~31% fasted, GSK1322322 57% fasted/77% fed, encainide mean ~42%) are above 20%; L5 gut-wall efflux records are mechanism-level, mixed, and not F measurements, and do not overturn those direct outcomes; low-F contexts are structurally dissimilar or low-transfer; unresolved uncertainty is captured as moderate confidence and evidence gaps."
}

